cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LunarAtlas in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "LunarAtlas: A Reproducible Data Processing and Interactive Visualization Infrastructure for Chandrayaan-3 LIBS Level-1 Archives"

abstract: >
  LunarAtlas is open-source software that turns the publicly archived Chandrayaan-3 laser-induced
  breakdown spectroscopy (LIBS) Level-1 (L1) products into relational, query-ready, L1-derived spectral
  records. It parses the PDS4 labels, verifies each data file against the checksum declared in its label,
  reshapes the 2,094-channel tables into long form, classifies plasma and background acquisitions from
  status flags, pairs each plasma acquisition with the most recent preceding background, subtracts and
  clamps, records pairing and clipping provenance, and serves the result through a REST API and a web
  viewer with LTTB downsampling that can preserve caller-specified channels. Wavelength coincidences with
  a short reference line list are provided for exploration only; the software does not identify elements
  or retrieve abundances. Software and documentation are available at:
  https://github.com/LovekeshAnand/LunarAtlas.

